  "body": "Window.close step 5 snapshots source snapshot params from the target top-level traversable active document. Step 6 then asks whether the incumbent navigable may navigate that target using those params, so the source sandbox flags are taken from the target instead of the caller.\n\nA script in a sandboxed child can consequently invoke top.close without its own sandboxed navigation flag affecting the decision. Ladybird encountered this while implementing https://github.com/LadybirdBrowser/ladybird/pull/12007.\n\nShould step 5 snapshot the incumbent global object associated Document, matching the source navigable used by the subsequent sandboxing check?",
